---
description: FastAPI backend conventions
globs: ["backend/**/*.py"]
alwaysApply: false
---
- Python 3.12, FastAPI, Pydantic v2, httpx, Pillow, rapidfuzz. Type-hint everything.
- Errors: raise `ApiError(status, code, message, fallback=...)`. Never return raw exceptions or stack traces.
- Every handler is reachable with `create_app(settings, ocr_provider)` so tests can inject fakes. No module-level global state beyond `app`.
- Logging: use `logging.getLogger("janrx")` with `extra={"fields": {...}}`. Request ID is automatic. No PII, no image data, no extracted text in logs.
- OCR providers implement `OcrProvider` (`app/ocr/base.py`). Add new providers there; select via `OCR_PROVIDER`.
- Tests are mocked (no network, no real model). Run `pytest -q` before finishing a task.
